# What never belongs in this repository.
#
# It used to be fifty-two rules naming individual files under a phase1..phase4
# layout that no longer exists -- `phase3/fast_ab_existing_surfaces/R61_AB_V1/
# fits-full-range/` and its like. None of those paths are here any more, so none
# of those rules protected anything; they were a record of a directory structure
# rather than a list of what to keep out. What is left is what is still true.

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# --- Node and the frontend build --------------------------------------------
node_modules/
panel/web/dist/
# TypeScript's incremental build cache. It was tracked, so every build produced
# a diff in a file nobody reads and every branch produced a conflict in it.
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Editors and operating systems ------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Credentials --------------------------------------------------------------
# Real env files never; the .example ones always, because they are the
# documentation of what a deployment needs.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!*.env.example
!.env.example

# --- State a deployment writes ------------------------------------------------
# Not source. These are what a running panel accumulates, and a commit that
# carries them makes one operator's deployment everybody else's starting state.
panel/config-versions/
panel/settings.local.json
panel/modules.json
panel/audit/

# --- Data ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Surfaces, runs and volumes. Gigabytes, reproducible from the pipeline, and
# belonging to a deployment rather than to the code. workspace/catalog is
# deliberately tracked: it is the catalogue, not the data it describes.
workspace/surfaces/
workspace/campaigns/
workspace/archive/
vendor/
.local/
